[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1957","stub":{"id":"1957","section":"Damascus to South Fork of the Holston River (U.S. 58)","altname":"","river":"Laurel Creek","difficulty":"IIplusstandoutIII","states":["USA-VRG"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"275","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The easiest put-in is just downstream of the Old Mill restaurant, with easy access and parking.  But you could also put in on Beaverdam Creek, if it has enough water, next to the red caboose.  The Beaverdam confluence is just downstream of the Old Mill.","id":"110253","location":{"latitude":"36.633326","longitude":"-81.785198"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":"N6wObWEvuf0rkmCgfZtJi","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"The Dam is located about two-thirds of the way down this run. You will see the horizon line after a long flat pool. You can run the Dam on the far left which is about a 7 ft drop or  on the far right which is scrapy slide drop of about 5 ft. You can also bang down the overflow channel on the right if its not blocked by debris.\n\nThere is currently a large tree blocking the left side of the dam which has revealed that the ledge is badly eroded and undercut. It almost looks man made but either way its definitely a cave like feature under there. We have ran this side many many times with out incident but just be aware!","id":"5660","location":{"latitude":"36.643122","longitude":"-81.820223"},"name":"Dam","distance":"2.33","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"12157"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Although Laurel Creek ends in about 3 miles when it flows into the South Fork Holston, most people continue another 4 miles to the Alvarado take-out (pictured) on the South Fork Holston, for a 7 mile trip.","id":"115515","location":{"latitude":"36.650447","longitude":"-81.832429"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"3.21","photoID":"NjzCJ3aaVQzIjzSlmNLEL","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"12159","ext":"mov","post_id":"6675","description":"","caption":"Jason/Dam","poi_name":"","subject":"Jason Bordwine","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12159","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12159"}},{"id":"7587","ext":"mov","post_id":"6676","description":"","caption":"Jason at the Dam","poi_name":"The Dam","subject":"Jason Bordwine","author":"Brian Combs","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7587","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7587"}},{"id":"7588","ext":"mov","post_id":"6676","description":"","caption":"Mike at the Dam","poi_name":"The Dam","subject":"Mike Sage","author":"Jason Bordwine","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7588","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7588"}},{"id":"7589","ext":"mov","post_id":"6676","description":"","caption":"Brian at the Dam","poi_name":"The Dam","subject":"Brian Combs","author":"Jason Bordwine","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7589","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7589"}},{"id":"8350","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7171","description":"Pretty typical rapid on this stretch of Laurel.  This creek is a lot of fun.  Lots of series of ledges and stuff to have fun on.  ","caption":"Laurel Fun","poi_name":"not sure","subject":"Brian Gillispie","author":"Travis Proffitt","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8350","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8350"}},{"id":"8351","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7171","description":"Here's Liz at the same spot on Laurel.  Guess we thought this rapid was photogenic.","caption":"Liz on Laurel","poi_name":"","subject":"Liz Daniels","author":"Travis Proffitt","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8351","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8351"}},{"id":"12156","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6675","description":"","caption":"4 Man Duckie!","poi_name":"Dam","subject":"Billy, Brian, Jason, Burton","author":"","poi_id":"5660","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12156","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12156"}},{"id":"12157","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6675","description":"","caption":"Jason at the Dam","poi_name":"Dam","subject":"Jason Bordwine","author":"","poi_id":"5660","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12157","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12157"}},{"id":"12154","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6675","description":"","caption":"Brian at the Dam","poi_name":"Dam","subject":"Brian Combs","author":"Jason Bordwine","poi_id":"5660","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12154","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12154"}},{"id":"879697","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880250","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Shawn Yates","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879697","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879697"}},{"id":"NjzCJ3aaVQzIjzSlmNLEL","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZP84BDHQK7PmjYoHRgwN0","description":"","caption":"Takeout on SF Holston, Alvarado","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Philip Young","poi_id":"115515","photo_date":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","updated_at":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/NjzCJ3aaVQzIjzSlmNLEL","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/NjzCJ3aaVQzIjzSlmNLEL"}},{"id":"N6wObWEvuf0rkmCgfZtJi","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZP84BDHQK7PmjYoHRgwN0","description":"","caption":"Put-in below Old Mill","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Philip Young","poi_id":"110253","photo_date":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","updated_at":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/N6wObWEvuf0rkmCgfZtJi","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/N6wObWEvuf0rkmCgfZtJi"}},{"id":"tYHi40secLR5IzVsx9RoA","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZP84BDHQK7PmjYoHRgwN0","description":"650 cfs","caption":"Laurel  Creek","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Philip Young","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","updated_at":"2024-03-30T16:37:20.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/tYHi40secLR5IzVsx9RoA","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/tYHi40secLR5IzVsx9RoA"}}],"detail":{"id":"1957","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Laurel Creek is the section of water that runs through the town of Damascus, VA. It is most commonly referred to as the lower section of Whitetop Laurel or the Upper Section of South Fork Holston. The run actually starts at the confluence of Whitetop Laurel Creek and Beaverdam Creek and continues down to where the South Fork Holston enters on the right. Laurel Creek can be run anywhere from a scrapy 300 cfs to as high as you feel comfortable. At levels above 1000 cfs there are many great surf waves and playspots. About two thirds of the way down after a long flat pool you will see a horizon line signaling you are at an old mill dam. You can scout on river right as the left side is private property. The best routes are on the far left and right sides or you can scrape down the overflow channel on the right side. Its best to put in for this section at the Park in Damascus. You will see the parking area, just look for the red Caboose. There are numerous takeout points but most paddlers combine this section with the South Fork Holston.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"2.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"1957","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"400","beginMediumRunnable":"700","beginHighRunnable":"1500","endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"S F HOLSTON RIVER NEAR DAMASCUS, VA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03473000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"275","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.98","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.65178127","longitude":"-81.8440102"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03473000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/03473000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"275","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["110253","5660","115515"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-81.790637,36.636778],[-81.791046,36.636761],[-81.791314,36.636787],[-81.791775,36.636907],[-81.791775,36.636907],[-81.792108,36.637329],[-81.792828,36.637884],[-81.792831,3